    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nFrom https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42000:\n> Any Lua code that keeps module-level state across keystrokes sees the side-effects of the previous replay(s), because the replay sandbox cannot isolate arbitrary Lua state.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSolution: per cursor state.\n\nAnd specifically state, and not something more general, like cursor instance id: if the cursor is deleted, it's state should also be cleaned up, while with an instance id, state stored in a separate table wont (unless the instance id is a gc-object, and table has metatable with `__mode='k'`).\n<br>\n\nFeature would help fixing: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42000",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-24T17:01:04Z",
    "closed_by": {
